description:
Design a pulse-width modulation (PWM) generator that modulates the output signal based on an 8-bit input value. The module operates with a clock frequency of 50 MHz and produces a PWM signal with a frequency of 1 kHz. The output will be HIGH for a duration proportional to the value of the input, determined by a threshold set every time the counter overflows. The circuit effectively converts the 8-bit digital input into a PWM signal, allowing for adjustable duty cycle control.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] in,
  output reg out // Changed 'out' to 'output reg' to allow assignment
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] in,
  output reg out // Changed 'out' to 'output reg' to allow assignment
);parameter clk_freq = 50000000; // 50 MHz
parameter pwm_freq = 1000; // 1 kHz

reg [31:0] counter = 0;
reg [7:0] threshold = 0;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter >= (clk_freq / pwm_freq)) begin
    counter <= 0;
    threshold <= in;
  end
  out <= (counter < threshold);
end

endmodule

