description:
Design a 2-bit greater-than comparator. The module outputs a HIGH signal (`agrb`) when the 2-bit input `a` is greater than the 2-bit input `b`. The comparison is achieved by evaluating several conditions: it first checks if the most significant bit of `a` is greater than that of `b`, then checks lower significance under specific circumstances, effectively implementing a hierarchical comparison logic.
module top_module(
    input  wire[1:0] a, b,
    output wire agrb
   );

code:
module top_module(
    input  wire[1:0] a, b,
    output wire agrb
   );wire p0, p1, p2;


   assign agrb = p0 | p1 | p2;

   assign p0 = a[1] & ~b[1];
   assign p1 = a[0] & ~b[1] & ~b[0];
   assign p2 = a[1] & a[0] & ~b[0];

endmodule

