description:
Design a priority encoder that takes an 8-bit input and produces a 3-bit output representing the highest priority input that is active. The output corresponds to the position of the highest active bit in the input, with lower indices having higher priority. If multiple bits are high, the encoder prioritizes the bit with the smallest index. The system updates the output on each rising edge of the clock signal.
