description:
Design a parity generator that computes the even parity for an n-bit input signal. The module takes an n-bit wide input and generates a single-bit output representing the parity. Specifically, it calculates the parity by XOR'ing all input bits together and inverts the result to produce the output. If the output is HIGH, it indicates an even number of HIGH input bits, making it suitable for error detection in digital communication systems.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output out
);parameter n = 8; // number of input signals

reg [n-1:0] in_reg;
reg parity;

integer i;
always @(*) begin
  in_reg = in;
  parity = 1'b0;
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    parity = parity ^ in_reg[i];
  end
end

assign out = ~parity;

endmodule

